// Mare Liberum · the doors of the web
// An agent that goes online with a task needs a door: an address it can open right now that answers the task, without a
// key, without an account and without a browser. This file is the hand-kept part of the routing table:
//   TOPICS — what a task is about, recognised by its words in many languages
//   DOORS  — open doors per topic: public JSON APIs first (the answer as data), then feeds and pages
// Every door carries a link with {q} and the word it was last tested with. The long tail (the search link of thousands
// of websites) lives in bangs-data.mjs. Doors are tested from the sea's own server; a door that stops opening fades.

// strip: words that name the shelf and only blur the search · hint: what an agent should know before it tries
// words: single words, any language (a word of five letters or more also matches as the beginning of a longer word);
